cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BRIEF-Acoustics in your research, please cite this software. If
  you use its non-singular Burton-Miller formulation, please also cite the
  preferred method paper below.
title: "BRIEF-Acoustics: acoustic non-singular boundary element method solver"
version: "0.1.0-alpha.1"
date-released: 2026-08-29
url: "https://github.com/sq-modelling/brief-acoustics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sq-modelling/brief-acoustics"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sun"
    given-names: "Qiang"
    affiliation: "RMIT University"
abstract: >-
  BRIEF-Acoustics is a research-preview acoustic non-singular boundary element
  method solver for frequency-domain Helmholtz problems. The current release
  includes a modern Fortran solver core, a non-singular Burton-Miller
  formulation, and a documented Python case-file workflow. Its validation set
  covers analytical Dirichlet, Neumann, and Robin sphere-scattering benchmarks,
  published fictitious-frequency regressions, and a non-spherical manufactured
  solution.
keywords:
  - boundary element method
  - non-singular boundary integral method
  - acoustics
  - Helmholtz equation
  - Burton-Miller method
  - scientific software validation
  - Fortran
  - Python
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
